abstract: >-
  Six dependent Isabelle/HOL sessions formalize cross-domain state
  preservation, regulatory action composition, authenticated message
  execution, reservation correctness and evidence-qualified terminal
  consumers, finite funding allocation and preservation of completed decisions
  through historical projection and recovery, while an independent
  PARTIAL / NO SAME research companion checks protected-behavior profile
  consequences without an Oraclizer implementation or product-refinement
  target. The repository covers
  deterministic selection and conditional aggregate progress, authenticated
  views, guarded model-level convergence, a degree-indexed hierarchy, complete
  action-pair classification, typed outcomes, trace and frame properties, and
  finite transformation normal forms, source-event credit uniqueness,
  representation equivalence and checked message summaries with explicit
  external assumptions and scope boundaries. The composition extension connects
  the existing source, financial and regulatory consumers to fresh completed
  calls and recovery of the same recorded executions; physical and compiled
  implementation correspondence remains outside these model results.
